# The patched RTX 30 kernels (sm86/build.py) that have run on an RTX 30 card, one line each:
#   <nvcc version> <hash> <what ran it>
# build.py writes qc_sm86_cubin.h only when what it built is listed here for the nvcc that built it, so a toolkit
# that compiles the kernel another way ships no patched kernel and the core runs the compiled one. The hash covers
# every section of the cubin but the names (build.py says how), so one line serves Linux and Windows builds.
# A line is added only after its file has run verify-core.js (all five checks) on an RTX 30 card through
# QUANTUS_CUDA_CUBIN_FILE, and the core's own startup check has passed there.

# QC_RED 3 with QC_DPRIME (goal/q3-rtx30 857458c0, 20 Nov), 158 tails; no longer built (QC_DM_T0, below). RTX 3070
# (Vast 61584429, 180 W cap): startup check passed, verify-core all five PASS (258.48 MH/s); a cubin with the tails
# left as compiled was refused by the startup check. RTX 3070 Ti: qrace 71.7% of SRBMiner 3.8.9, 9 shares accepted.
